    "pressure": {
      "file": "online_condition_monitoring_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Health status at a glance: OK – warning – alarm",
      "description": "Permanently installed sensors send vibration, temperature and oil-condition data at intervals (seconds to hours) through a gateway to a historian and analytics. Trends against baselines and alarm limits flag developing faults weeks ahead (P–F interval), so repairs are planned instead of reacting to breakdowns. Here the fan is healthy (green), the pump shows a rising trend (amber), and the gearbox oil sensor reports wear debris (red). Wireless sensors trade data rate / battery life against detail; critical machines still use wired protection systems (API 670).",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
